{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC evidence (kept in this comment, not the description, so the plan-review attestation stays current — ticking a box is attestation-safe, adding prose is not):\nAC1 — seam-spy on _confirm.emit/emit_text in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py, parametrized over create/link/transition: exactly ONE routed line per dispatch and stdout == that line + newline (nothing printed outside the seam), plus a no-op variant (re-link, already-at-status transition). Proven to bite: replacing confirm_created's emit_text with a bare print makes create fail 'routed 0 lines through the shared seam'. test_confirmation_formatters_need_no_store covers the no-follow-up-store-read half by formatting with cwd in an empty tmp dir and REBAR_ROOT unset.\nAC2 — MUTATION_VERBS in scripts/gen_cli_reference.py, 17 rows == _WRITES_FULL | _LIFECYCLE, rendered as the 'Verb inventory: no-op-capable vs always-writes' table in the generated docs/cli-reference.md. _check_mutation_verbs() makes render() raise on drift from rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails on an unclassified verb); test_an_unclassified_verb_fails_the_generator asserts that behaviour by deleting a row.\nAC3 — 'Confirmation-line record (pre-42cd70b889 -> today)' table in docs/cli-reference.md from the same curated rows; old strings read out of 42cd70b889^ rather than paraphrased.\nAC4 — make lint PASS (complexity active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0), make typecheck PASS (572 files), full tests/unit 5077 passed / 7 skipped. Gerrit change 1933 merged as 0c1906abc9 with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments. One non-blocking review advisory (already marked resolved by the bot): the 'stdout carries nothing the seam emitted' invariant has a documented exception on link's REDIRECT path, which the merged test test_link_redirect_record_is_byte_identical_and_sole_stdout_result covers and this new test deliberately does not exercise."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787190191592982001,"uuid":"7d6011ec-47b1-4d90-bf5e-de8c3f7ae0f5"}